Coverage map: frontmatter-parses -> real_bboxy_frontmatter_parses and malformed nested-source negative fixture; #48 -> complete positive/invalid diagnostic matrix, duplicate/missing corpus numbers, numeric/slug/id/path and legacy heading resolution, and the actual next-number script. licenses-present -> real license fixture script. document-viewer Markdown/Build order -> semantic AST, UTF-8 offsets, source-preserving diagnostics, wrapping, rich tables, header projection and retained links. Mermaid -> real corpus/native drawing and unchanged fixtures/lab include_str! comparisons. No invariant check or spec acceptance line loses a test.

Deleted record_number_is_a_positive_integer_metadata_value is covered input-for-input by invalid_explicit_record_numbers_keep_their_source_and_show_a_diagnostic: the same seven invalid values, valid 47 and absent number, plus typed metadata value/source retention and diagnostic location. This is the sole deletion.

The corpus Mermaid check enumerates sorted real Markdown paths directly without following symlink directories; unlike git ls-files, it also checks new local records. The external next-number and licensing processes remain because they exercise those public scripts, with no in-memory equivalent. User-visible source-fallback notes remain specified output, not a low-level error-prose test.

